# TodoTask IDE Rules (Compatibility)

This file mirrors the project coding rules for editors that still read `.cursorrules`.

## Global

- Follow `docs/baseline.md` as highest authority.
- Check `docs/dev-phases.md` before new implementation.
- Package manager: pnpm only.

## Frontend (`packages/frontend`)

- Vue 3 with `<script setup lang="ts">` only; no Options API.
- TypeScript business code only; no `.js` business files.
- No `any`.
- Component naming: PascalCase file names and PascalCase usage in template.
- Composables prefix `use`; handler functions prefix `handle`.
- Do not use `v-if` and `v-for` on same element.
- Never use array index as `v-for` key.
- Route lazy loading with dynamic import.
- Prefer Tailwind; use Less for complex cases.
- Private component style should be `scoped`; use `:deep()` when needed.

## Backend (`packages/backend`)

- Strict dependency flow: Handler -> Service -> Repository.
- Handler only handles request/response mapping.
- Service handles business logic and business errors.
- Repository handles MongoDB CRUD only.
- Never ignore `error`.
- Use Zap for logs; no `fmt.Println` for logging.
- Use unified response style from `pkg/response`.
- DB operations must carry `context.Context` and timeout control.
- No physical delete for business entities.
- No unmanaged fire-and-forget goroutines.

## Git

- Commit message format: `<type>(<scope>): <中文说明>` (<= 25 chars in summary).
- Do not push without explicit user authorization.

